It gives you the energy.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:21.220
Jeff, I consider you one of the
best actors in the business.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.489
-Big statement.
-Well, I do.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:24.824
I do, and --
-Well, thank you.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.693
-I was trying out some
characters in the monologue,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.561
and I just -- and I think --

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.463
I don't know.
I just want, maybe, your notes.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.898
-For the baseball-bat thing?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.967
You saw it?
-I thought it was good.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.101
-You did, right?

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.469
Did you believe
that I was a bookie?

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.805
-It had -- Well, it had --
If Jerry Lewis was a bookie.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:39.939
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.875
It had that kind of --
"Baseball bat"!

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.745
-"Baseball bat!"
But that keeps you guessing.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.446
You go, "Hey, is this guy
gonna break my legs?"

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:48.581
-Exactly.
-You don't know, it keeps you --

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.682
-Which is what you want.
-Thank you, yeah.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.916
I didn't get the part, but --

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.018
You know...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.420
Again, I could do
lots of different things.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.289
If there's, like, an extra
in "To Kill a Mockingbird"

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.690
or something like that,
I'm down the street.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.791
-Sure, sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.159
-You know,
you need someone to come on,

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.762
just give me a line.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.930
-Give you a line?
-Sure.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.366
Give me a line, I'll do it.
-Uh, uh, uh...

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.501
-And you're Atticus, right?
-Yeah, I'm Atticus.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.571
Uh, uh...
-What do you want, Mr. Ewell?

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.973
-Okay. Ready.
Oh, I'm Mr. Ewell?

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.941
-You're Bob Ewell.
You're the bad guy.

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:18.745
-Mr. Ewell was my dad.
Call me Bob.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.480
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.582
How about that?
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.951 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.085
Improvising.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.820
"What do you want, Mr. Ewell?",

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:28.921
and then Mr. Ewell turns,
and he goes,

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.290
"Mr. Ewell's my father.
Call me Bob."

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.291
[ Laughter ]
Right?

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.726
-Sure.
-Yeah, don't --

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.960
You think about it.
I'm down the street.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.263
I'll give you my cell again.
-The part is cast.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.598
The part is cast, unfortunately.
-The part is cast.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.735
I saw that you and your wife --
You were recently --

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:46.572
You were in the press because
she threw out the first pitch.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.440
It was interesting.
Because you were supposed to

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:51.076
throw out the first pitch
at a Pittsburgh Pirates game?

00:01:51.076 --> 00:01:52.312
-We were shooting
"American Rust"

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:55.681
in Pittsburgh, yes.
-Did she know at all?

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:57.283
-The Pira--
We called the Pirates,

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.152
and, you know, being one of
the few celebrities

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.354
in Pittsburgh at the moment,
they said yes.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.489
And they said, "We'll put you
in the suite with the owner,"

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.524
and I said,
"Well, it's my wife's birthday.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.327
Could you just get her a cake
in the suite?

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.128
Maybe the mascot could show up."

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:11.230
'Cause we've been married
42 years.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.565
[ Cheers and applause ]
I'm -- I'm --

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.368
Well, but...

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.469
I have run out of ideas.
-You're out of ideas.

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:19.472
-There is nothing.
She's going,

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:22.608
"How about a little --"
I said, "No, no, I'm done.

00:02:22.608 --> 00:02:25.211
I can't." And then I said,
"A cake, maybe the mascot.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.213
I might get away
with the birthday that way."

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.948
We're walking
into the Pirates thing,

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.283
and the Pirates P.R. people
are there, and they said,

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:34.187
"Would you like your wife
to throw out the first pitch?"

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.589
And I said,
"Yes, and don't tell her."

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.525
[ Laughter ]
So, we get there,

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:42.195
and we get to the dugout, and we
go, "Okay, Jeff, it's time."

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.596
And I go,
"All right, Kathleen, come on."

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.031
She goes, "What?" I'm like,
"Come on, come on, come on."

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.234
And she is from
the upper peninsula of Michigan,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.370
so she can dig in and go,
"I ain't moving.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.606
I ain't moving.
No, this is not happening."

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.675
So I'm dragging her,
and she starts to go --

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.010
Now we get out to the --
Now we're out to the mound,

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.245
and I have the ball,
and she goes,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.612
"What am I doing out here?"

00:03:00.612 --> 00:03:03.316
I said, "Here, you're gonna
throw the first pitch."

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.017
-In front of everybody.
-And then I -- yeah.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:07.119
And we've got, you know, fans --
-Stadium.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:10.289
Maybe 15,000, I don't know.
And so I'm backing up.

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:12.825
And she's going, "I can't
believe you're doing this."

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.293
[ Laughter ]
"What are you doing?"

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:17.696
-42 years, that's right.
-And I'm to the home plate,

00:03:17.696 --> 00:03:21.501
and now I'm going, "Oh, my God.
I gotta catch it,"

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.771
because if she throws it and
actor boy doesn't catch it...

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.706
-Oh, then the whole bit's --
-Then it's viral.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:30.276
So now I'm just --
So, I'm like those guys

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.245
at the tarmac
when the plane's coming in,

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.780
with the orange, I'm going,
"Anywhere in here!"

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.383
[ Laughter ]
"Anywhere in here!"

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.918
-Anywhere, yeah.
Of course.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.921
-"I love you, honey!
I'm sorry I did this!"

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.089
-"I'm begging you."

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:47.593
-And she does one of these,
and then she threw it.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:50.229
-We have the video.
Let's take a look at the video.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:54.333
Here we go.

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:57.202
-Yeah! Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.202 --> 00:04:00.773
That is love.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:04.410
That's love right there.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.478
I want to talk about
"American Rust."

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:08.247
It's on Showtime.
It's fantastic.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.016
I've seen two episodes,
I believe.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:14.353
-I love stories about
small-town people but told

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.622
not in a way that Hollywood does
where they come in

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:19.158
and polish it up and, you know,
Hollywood people come --

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.126
You know, it's like, I want you
to feel like you're in the town.

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:22.729
So it's real.
Authentic.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:26.032
And the writing on it
is so strong.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:29.702
These are good people,
decent people who are just

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:33.272
trying to survive, and they're
making some bad choices.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.441
There's a murder involved,
and --

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.244
But it's more about
the people around it.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.780
And it's just -- I got some
really good people in it.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.982
And I'm real proud of it.
The first three episodes

00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:46.285
that have been up are just,
like, the setup.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.221
What happens later is just --
you can't even --

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.389
you don't even --
-Oh, really?

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:51.123
-You think you know
what's gonna happen --

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.524
-I think I do.
-Pwooo!

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.694
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, it's one of those.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:57.430
So I'm real excited about it.
-Oh, wow.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.197
I'm even more excited now,
because I'm invested.

